WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:06.840
It seems like every other major movie these
days is a prequel, sequel, remake, or reboot.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:10.360
But they're not all just barely warmed-up
leftovers.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:15.860
Some upcoming remakes and reboots just might
be worth your time — or, dare we say, blow

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:17.040
you away.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:23.340
Shaft

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:30.300
In 1971, MGM released a film adaptation of
Ernest Tidyman's detective novel Shaft ...

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:31.900
"Shut yo mouth."

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:36.740
Uh, we're just talking about the original
Shaft, starring Richard Roundtree.

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:42.390
In 2000, Paramount remade the film with John
Singleton directing and Samuel L. Jackson

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.230
starring in the leading role.

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:48.900
And now, New Line Cinema is looking to release
another fresh take.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:55.040
The new film has Black-ish creator Kenya Barris
and The Goldbergs producer Alex Barnow writing

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:58.610
the script, with Ride Along director Tim Story
at the helm.

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:03.850
Hiring comedy writers and directors may concern
some Shaft fans, but producer John Davis says

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:07.050
the movie won't strictly be a comedy.

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:09.140
"Can you dig it?"

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:11.680
Universal's Monsterverse

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:16.580
Shared universes are the big thing in Hollywood
these days, and Universal Pictures is the

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:18.890
latest studio to get in on the action.

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:24.600
But instead of turning to the comics for inspiration,
they're building a shared monster universe

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:31.159
— a monsterverse, if you will — centering
on the studio's iconic movie monsters of old.

00:01:31.159 --> 00:01:36.390
It all begins with Alex Kurtzman's new take
on The Mummy, starring Tom Cruise and Russell

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:37.390
Crowe.

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:42.360
Hopefully, the finished film will have all
of its sound, unlike the botched first trailer

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:43.800
"Ahhh."

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:50.299
That never gets old.

00:01:50.299 --> 00:01:56.159
Rounding out the "Monsterverse" is Bride of
Frankenstein, with Javier Bardem playing Frankenstein's

00:01:56.159 --> 00:01:57.159
monster …

00:01:57.159 --> 00:01:59.090
Invisible Man, starring Johnny Depp ....

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:04.600
An overhauled Wolf Man, with Dwayne Johnson
reportedly being eyed for the title role …

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:08.700
A new Van Helsing, said to be in the vein
of Mad Max ...

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:14.090
And finally, Creature from the Black Lagoon,
potentially starring Scarlett Johansson … as

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:16.700
the female lead, not the creature.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:21.290
Of course, she does have the experience to
play the creature if need be...

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:23.450
Disney's live-action remakes

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:29.480
After seeing enormous success with Tim Burton's
Alice in Wonderland in 2010, Disney commissioned

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:34.890
more live-action remakes based on their animated
classics, like 2016's Jungle Book adaptation.

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:40.280
Beauty and the Beast racked up record-breaking
grosses in March 2017 with a live-action take

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:42.760
on the story starring Emma Watson.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:48.279
Next, Jon Favreau will try to build on his
success with The Jungle Book by remaking The

00:02:48.279 --> 00:02:49.290
Lion King.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:54.900
After that, Disney's lined up — *deep breath*
— Mulan, Aladdin, Cruella, Dumbo, Genies,

00:02:54.900 --> 00:03:00.799
Peter Pan, Pinocchio, Tink, The Little Mermaid,
and a lot more, all in live-action.

00:03:00.799 --> 00:03:05.620
With an impressive collection of planned problems
like that, at least two or three might actually

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:07.129
be good!

00:03:07.129 --> 00:03:08.129
It

00:03:08.129 --> 00:03:13.340
Stephen King's classic It was made into a
two-part miniseries for ABC in 1990, starring

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:16.430
Tim Curry as the monstrous Pennywise the Clown.

00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:21.749
Eager to offer a scarier, more lavish adaptation,
Hollywood filmmakers have attempted to bring

00:03:21.749 --> 00:03:24.219
the novel to life on the big screen for years.

00:03:24.219 --> 00:03:30.209
Beasts of No Nation and True Detective director
Cary Fukunaga led the charge for several years

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:35.040
before dropping the project in 2015 following
budgetary concerns with New Line Cinema.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:40.919
Now, Mama director Andy Muschietti has taken
up directing duties, with Bill Skarsgård

00:03:40.919 --> 00:03:42.209
playing Pennywise.

00:03:42.209 --> 00:03:45.430
Producer Dan Lin likens the remake to Netflix's
Stranger Things:

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:50.219
"It's very much an homage to '80s movies,
whether it's classic Stephen King or even

00:03:50.219 --> 00:03:51.459
Spielberg."

00:03:51.459 --> 00:03:52.459
The Crow

00:03:52.459 --> 00:03:57.549
Several non-superhero comic book movies have
done remarkably well over the years — including

00:03:57.549 --> 00:04:01.260
1994's The Crow, starring the late Brandon
Lee.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:04.889
But for years, Hollywood has tried to remake
The Crow to no avail.

00:04:04.889 --> 00:04:10.629
That may all be about to change: Jason Momoa
signed on to the film in 2016, with The Hallow's

00:04:10.629 --> 00:04:12.199
Corin Hardy directing.

00:04:12.199 --> 00:04:17.329
But with the remake having moved from Relativity
Media to Davis Films and renamed The Crow

00:04:17.329 --> 00:04:22.109
Reborn, there's uncertainty as to whether
Momoa and Hardy will remain on board.

00:04:22.109 --> 00:04:27.940
We'll know soon: the film is finally scheduled
to begin production sometime in 2017.

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:29.389
Escape from New York

00:04:29.389 --> 00:04:34.639
Set in a dystopian future, John Carpenter's
1981 classic Escape from New York follows

00:04:34.639 --> 00:04:40.169
Kurt Russell's Snake Plissken, tasked with
finding the President of the United States

00:04:40.169 --> 00:04:44.770
after Air Force One crash-lands in Manhattan
— which the government has turned into an

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:47.770
enormous maximum security prison.

00:04:47.770 --> 00:04:52.669
Warner Bros. has spent years pursuing fruitless
attempts to put together a remake.

00:04:52.669 --> 00:04:56.879
Producer Joel Silver's the latest to take
a crack at it, and he wants to not only remake

00:04:56.879 --> 00:05:02.050
the film but turn it into a trilogy that's
reportedly in the vein of Rise of the Planet

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:09.440
of the Apes and — inspired by the 2011 video
game Batman: Arkham City, of all things.

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:10.440
Tomb Raider

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:15.370
Aside from the half-dozen Resident Evil movies,
Tomb Raider is likely the next most successful

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:20.990
video game movie franchise ever made, thanks
to the two Angelina Jolie films from the early

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:21.990
2000s.

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:26.490
Warner Bros. is looking to reboot Tomb Raider
on the big screen, with Academy Award-winning

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:31.990
actress Alicia Vikander as Lara Croft and
Justified's Walton Goggins as the villain.

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:36.699
As Goggins puts it, the film will be like
"Raiders of the Lost Ark meets a genre version

00:05:36.699 --> 00:05:40.580
of the Joseph Conrad novel Victory: An Island
Tale."

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:45.199
Though not much is known about the story,
we do know it will closely follow the gritty

00:05:45.199 --> 00:05:50.990
new video game series, which find a young
Lara Croft on a quest to find her father.

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:52.300
Ocean's Eight

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:58.030
After remaking Lewis Milestone's original
Ocean's Eleven from 1960, Steven Soderbergh

00:05:58.030 --> 00:06:00.830
followed up with two more successful installments.

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:06.030
But the cast and crew opted not to make a
fourth film due to Bernie Mac's untimely death.

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:10.729
Instead of another sequel, Warner Bros. has
decided to simply reboot the series with an

00:06:10.729 --> 00:06:12.800
all-female cast.

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:19.830
Helmed by Hunger Games director Gary Ross,
Ocean's Eight will star — *here we go* — Sandra

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:24.660
Bullock, Cate Blanchett, Helena Bonham Carter,
Anne Hathaway, Dakota Fanning, Rihanna, Sarah

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:27.800
Paulson, Mindy Kaling ... and Matt Damon?

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:29.659
"Matt Damon!"

00:06:29.659 --> 00:06:34.629
Damon is set to reprise his role from the
original Ocean's trilogy as Linus Caldwell.

00:06:34.629 --> 00:06:38.250
The film's scheduled to arrive in June 2018.

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:39.250
Thanks for watching!

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:41.900
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:44.479
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

